{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:5163-1","published":"2026-11-10T09:42:45Z","modified":"2026-11-10T20:30:03.943540466Z","related":["CVE-2026-103658","CVE-2026-75818","CVE-2026-75819","CVE-2026-75820"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-103658","CVE-2026-75818","CVE-2026-75819","CVE-2026-75820"],"summary":"Security update for aspell","details":"This update for aspell fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-75818: heap-based buffer overflow in the decompressor in `prog/prezip.c` can lead to memory corruption and\n  process crash (bsc#1284337).\n- CVE-2026-75819: out-of-bounds read in `ReadOnlyDict::load()` of `readonly_ws.cpp` can lead to heap memory disclosure\n  or application crash (bsc#1284338).\n- CVE-2026-75820: integer truncation in `WritableDict::add() ` of ` modules/speller/default/writable.cpp` can lead to\n  heap corruption (bsc#1284339).\n- CVE-2026-103658: Arbitrary code execution via crafted dictionary file (bsc#1285066).\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"aspell","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Server 12 SP5-LTSS","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/aspell&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Server%2012%20SP5-LTSS"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0.60.6.1-18.18.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"aspell":"0.60.6.1-18.18.1","aspell-devel":"0.60.6.1-18.18.1","aspell-ispell":"0.60.6.1-18.18.1","libaspell15":"0.60.6.1-18.18.1","libaspell15-32bit":"0.60.6.1-18.18.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2026:5163-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"aspell","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Server LTSS Extended Security 12 SP5","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/aspell&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Server%20LTSS%20Extended%20Security%2012%20SP5"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0.60.6.1-18.18.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"aspell":"0.60.6.1-18.18.1","aspell-devel":"0.60.6.1-18.18.1","aspell-ispell":"0.60.6.1-18.18.1","libaspell15":"0.60.6.1-1